Evelyn heard the beginning of her name, and then there was a sharp sound almost like something cracking in the distance. But instead of announcing her, Margaret set the ribbon down next to Tyler's pie and said, "Tyler Nguyen; a fine example of people trying new things." She paused. "We also have a pie here made from store-bought dough. It's unspectacular, as the judges agreed. But there's a first time for everything, and the runner-up ribbon for this year goes to—Evelyn Parrish."

Evelyn looked around. People were clapping. There was a tinny applause coming from the audiotape they were recording. Her chest felt tight.

Margaret offered the blue-and-white ribbon with a smile, and Evelyn took it.

"Thank you," Margaret said.

When the applause ended, Tyler Nguyen said loudly, "But I built that from scratch!"

